# strongSwan PKCS#11 plugin — ML-DSA/SLH-DSA/Ed448/Ed25519/ML-KEM PQC extension
#
# Generated 2026-08-08 (upgrade plan B6), regenerated 2026-09-02 (fix/
# strongswan-ed25519 — the previous regeneration predated G5's Ed448 wiring
# and this branch's Ed25519 wiring, so it was stale: applying it reproduced
# an EARLIER connector without either, contradicting tests/README.md's own
# documented 7/7-then-8/8 pass transcripts. Always regenerate with
# regen-strongswan-pkcs11-patch.sh after editing anything under
# strongswan-pkcs11/, or whenever the pinned strongSwan version bumps — do
# not assume this file is current just because it applies cleanly.
#
# Replaces a wholesale `COPY pqctoday-hsm/strongswan-pkcs11 .../plugins/pkcs11`
# in Dockerfile.network that silently discarded upstream changes to any file
# it overwrote — discovered 2026-08-08 when 6.0.7 renamed OID_SECT*R1 to
# OID_SECP*R1 and removed the old names inside this same directory; a naive
# COPY-based bump would have shipped 6.0.7 while keeping the pre-rename names,
# which would not even compile. Applying via `patch -p1` instead means a
# future upstream change to any of these modified files surfaces as a fuzzy
# hunk or an outright failure, not silence.
#
# Modified from upstream (6 files):
#   src/libstrongswan/plugins/pkcs11/Makefile.am          (+pkcs11_kem.{c,h} to SOURCES)
#   src/libstrongswan/plugins/pkcs11/pkcs11.h             (ML-DSA/SLH-DSA/ML-KEM mechanism + key type decls)
#   src/libstrongswan/plugins/pkcs11/pkcs11_dh.c          (ML-KEM key agreement path; MODP DH deregistered — see pkcs11_plugin.c)
#   src/libstrongswan/plugins/pkcs11/pkcs11_plugin.c      (PLUGIN_PROVIDE for KEY_ML_DSA_*/SLH_DSA_*/ED448/ED25519, KE ML_KEM_512/768/1024)
#   src/libstrongswan/plugins/pkcs11/pkcs11_private_key.c (ML-DSA/SLH-DSA sign via CKM_ML_DSA/CKM_SLH_DSA; Ed448/Ed25519 via CKM_EDDSA)
#   src/libstrongswan/plugins/pkcs11/pkcs11_public_key.c  (ML-DSA/SLH-DSA/Ed448/Ed25519 verify + SPKI decode; OID_SECP*R1 usage)
#
# New files, not present upstream (4 files):
#   src/libstrongswan/plugins/pkcs11/pkcs11_kem.{c,h}     (CKM_ML_KEM encapsulate/decapsulate wiring, all 3 sizes)
#   src/libstrongswan/plugins/pkcs11/test_ss.c            (standalone PKCS#11 smoke test)
#   src/libstrongswan/plugins/pkcs11/README.md            (fork notes)
#
# The other 13 files in strongswan-pkcs11/ (pkcs11_creds.*, pkcs11_hasher.*,
# pkcs11_library.*, pkcs11_manager.*, pkcs11_plugin.h, pkcs11_private_key.h,
# pkcs11_public_key.h, pkcs11_rng.*, pkcs11_dh.h) are byte-identical to
# upstream and are intentionally NOT part of this patch — they come from the
# strongSwan tarball unmodified, so an upstream change to any of them is a
# real, visible diff the next time this patch is regenerated, rather than an
# invisible overwrite.
#
